1. As well as
Example:

The students as well as the teacher did his/their work.

Correct:

✅ The students as well as the teacher did their work.

Why?

The main subject is:

The students

as well as the teacher is additional information.

So the pronoun refers to students → plural → their.

Important:

A as well as B → verb/pronoun generally agrees with A, not B.

Examples:

Ram as well as his friends has completed his work. ✅

Ram's friends as well as Ram have completed their work. ✅


2. One of those + plural noun + who

This is a very important SSC pattern.

He was one of those students who completed his/their project on time.

Correct:

✅ He was one of those students who completed their project on time.

Why?

who refers to those students, not just “he.”

Structure:

one of those students → plural

Therefore:

their project.

Compare:

He was one of those students who completed their projects.

Meaning:

He was one among several students who completed their projects.

So their is the traditional exam answer.

3. Neither...nor

This is where proximity becomes important.

Neither Ram nor his friends brought his/their documents.

Correct:

✅ Neither Ram nor his friends brought their documents.

Why?

With:

Neither A nor B

the pronoun/verb generally agrees with the nearer subject B.

Here:

Ram → singular
his friends → plural

The nearer subject is his friends.

Therefore:

their documents.


4. The treasurer and secretary

This one depends on whether the two nouns refer to one person or two different people.

Without repeated article:

The treasurer and secretary gave his/their consent.

This can indicate one person with two roles:

the treasurer and secretary

So:

✅ his consent.

The person is both the treasurer and secretary.

With repeated article:

The treasurer and the secretary gave his/their consent.

Now there are normally two different people:

the treasurer
and
the secretary

Therefore:

✅ their consent.




